# 0007 (v2, replaces 0007-memexport-readback-guard) - export pending mirror (Gears 3 chat, 2026-10-23; base 27958a8)
# Gears 3 "vertex explosions" come from random background NPCs (Shagg), in corridors where 10k-38k vertex ranges per
# 300 frames are read from memexport output (play log 20261023-005759) - NPCs skinned through memexport [G].
# Race (Gears 2 chat 01:09 + ours, [V by reading code]): exported pages are GPU-current only until a CPU store anywhere
# in the same 4 MB block (guest_watch.cpp bumps the whole block); UploadVertexSlot then uploads guest memory over them -
# but guest memory gets the export's bytes only when PollExportReadbacks lands them a frame or more later, so consumer
# draws read the PRE-export bytes in between.
# Switch --gow2_renderer_export_pending_mirror (default false = as before). On: pages covered by a readback still in
# flight keep feeding vertex fetches from the mirror (no upload over them); counted in a summary line.
# v1's per-page readback guard is dropped: it relied on GpuCurrent(), which the same 4 MB bumps make unreliable.
# Also corrects PollExportReadbacks' comment: TranslatePhysical writes raise no watch callback [V rexglue xmemory.h].
# Known gap (left): a late readback still overwrites bytes the CPU wrote after the export (xenia-edge dropped readback).
# Syntax-checked (Windows), not built or run. Applies on 27958a8 with or without 0004-0006.
diff -ruN a/src/layer0_xenos/renderer/shadow_renderer.cpp b/src/layer0_xenos/renderer/shadow_renderer.cpp
--- a/src/layer0_xenos/renderer/shadow_renderer.cpp	2026-10-23 01:16:56.089767115 -0700
+++ b/src/layer0_xenos/renderer/shadow_renderer.cpp	2026-10-23 01:17:07.873613748 -0700
@@ -155,6 +155,12 @@
                     "mirror (u0), export-only draws (no rasterization) run as point lists with no targets, the written "
                     "ranges become GPU-current and later vertex fetches read them from the mirror. false: such draws "
                     "are skipped, as before");
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(gow2_renderer_export_pending_mirror, false, "Gears2",
+                    "Patch 0007 (Gears 3 2026-10-23, NPC vertex explosions; race found by both chats): while an "
+                    "exported range's readback has not landed in guest memory yet, its pages keep feeding vertex "
+                    "fetches from the mirror (the export's bytes) even when a CPU write elsewhere in the same 4 MB block "
+                    "ended their GPU-current state - instead of re-uploading the pre-export guest bytes over them. "
+                    "false = as before");
 REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(gow2_renderer_memexport_readback, true, "Gears2",
                     "With --gow2_renderer_memexport: copy every exported range back into guest memory once the GPU has "
                     "written it (job 041: Gears 3 moves DXT textures with memexport copies, and DXT textures load from "
